Reciprocal pronouns show that two or more people/things do something to each other mutually.

There are two reciprocal pronouns:

each other
one another


1. EACH OTHER

Traditionally:

Each other → two persons/things

Examples:

The two cats were fighting with each other. ✅

There are two cats, so traditionally we use each other.

Ram and Shyam help each other. ✅

There are two people.

Meaning

Ram helps Shyam.
Shyam helps Ram.

So:

Ram and Shyam help each other.


2. ONE ANOTHER

Traditionally:

One another → more than two persons/things

Example:

All the students of the class help one another. ✅

There are more than two students.

Meaning:

Student A helps B, C, D...
B helps A, C, D...
etc.

3. Rani Ma'am's example: “knees”

He was so afraid that his knees knocked against each other. ✅

Why each other?

Because we are talking about two knees:

left knee
right knee

Therefore:

his knees knocked against each other
